--- parse -- generic string parsing for the handl runtime.
---
--- Contract surface for the `parse` stdlib interface: 1 function
--- covering parsing of a string into a `serde_json::Value` via a
--- caller-supplied parser. The `cap`/`op`/`handle` decls below declare
--- the capability and signature surface; `plugin-lib-stdlib`'s `parse`
--- `ModuleSpec` loads this file via `include_str!` (the `parse` module
--- row lists `parse.parse` in `ops`).
---
--- There is no native impl: the callable is the pure-handl export at the
--- bottom — it invokes the `parse` arrow on the parser record it's
--- handed (parser tokens are produced by the `url_rfc`/`url_whatwg`
--- modules). The old `DynParser`/`plugin-lib-parse`/`ops.rs` path is
--- gone.
---
--- ## Capability declarations (ADR-0077 Phase 4)
--- parse.parse -- parse a string into a value using a named parser.
cap "parse.parse"
op "parse.parse" : (String * Value) ~> Value
  guarantee: True
handle "parse.parse" with parse

--- Parser dispatch: the parser object is a record carrying a `parse`
--- arrow — produced by `url_rfc.url_rfc`/`url_whatwg.url_whatwg`/…
export parse := (input, parser) ~> (parser.parse)(input)
